preConditionHook:
// DID THE NEW EXTREME FIND MORE BUYERS THAN SELLERS? The best high of the last
// confirmBars bars is at least scalpTicks above the highest high of the
// swingLookback bars that came BEFORE them -- enough follow-through for the
// breakout traders to have taken a scalper's profit, which is R04-01's test of
// trend strength. Mirrored on the lows for the short side. Re-evaluated every
// bar, so it doubles as a rolling strength gauge.
//
// LEVELS ARE highest/lowest WINDOWS, not swing pivots: the candidate says swing
// high, and the merge re-expressed it over fixed windows because that needs no
// pivot detection and is the cheaper definition.
//
// BOTH WINDOWS ARE WRITTEN OUT in both twins as the Extremes scan that
// highest/lowest bottom out in -- seeded at the window's FIRST bar, the rest
// scanned with a strict comparison -- because the older window is
// highest(high, swingLookback)[confirmBars], a history reference at an INPUT
// offset; the same open-coding FailedBreakoutReversal uses. Extremes is EL
// source, so its comparisons carry the measured 2.22e-12 relational tolerance,
// hence el_gt / el_lt rather than raw > and <. Only the value is read, so the
// tie rule (an equal extreme keeps the earliest bar) cannot show. Seeding at the
// first bar also keeps each loop's start at or below its end for every input of
// 1 or more, so the EL twin's loops can never run backwards.
//
// The negation -- a new extreme that reverses within a bar or two -- is the
// other half of Brooks's sentence and is reached with the per-placement negate
// toggle, not a second rule.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables entry,
// never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
// Deepest bar touched: confirmBars + swingLookback - 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
recentHigh = high[0];
recentLow = low[0];
for (int i = 0; i <= (int)confirmBars - 1; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], recentHigh)) recentHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], recentLow)) recentLow = low[i];
}
priorHigh = high[(int)confirmBars];
priorLow = low[(int)confirmBars];
for (int i = (int)confirmBars; i <= (int)confirmBars + (int)swingLookback - 1; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorHigh)) priorHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorLow)) priorLow = low[i];
}
